why: stage 1 built DESCRIBE and only stage 4 has read it (a deployment
  naming a probe path). The backlog entry says NOT to start this as
  "generate OpenAPI", because an OpenAPI document has no in-repo
  consumer and a lane with no caller is the trap this arc has recorded
  three times. It says: name the consumer first.

  The consumer is the DOCUMENTATION. `docs/modules/okay-ops.md` lists
  the endpoints in prose, and prose drifts — that is precisely what
  stage 4 found between `Ops` and `Site`, and what the repository
  already solved elsewhere with committed renderings and a drift test
  ("two committed deploy renderings, each with its own drift test").

what: `Router.markdown` renders a table from the same entries that
  dispatch, and a test asserts the block committed in the module docs
  is what the live router renders. A route cannot then be served and
  undocumented, or documented and unserved — the property `describe`
  was built for, finally load-bearing.

  okay-ops, okay-demo and okay-chat all have Routers now, so there is
  something real to render.

not in scope: OpenAPI. When a consumer for it exists, the input is
  ready — `describe`, `params`, `queries` and the entry's body schema.

next: the renderer, the doc blocks, the drift test, docs
